WEBVTT

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.980
<i>The time is one hundred years ago.</i>

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.230
<i>Jean was worried about Nadia who was suffering from a stomachache,</i>

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.860
<i>so he set out to find herbs for her.</i>

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:36.280
<i>He lost consciousness when he ate some strange mushrooms.</i>

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:42.240
<i>In the evening, overwhelmed with gratitude, Nadia kissed him.</i>

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.410
<i>This was Jean's first kiss.</i>

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.710
<i>Just what is Nadia thinking?</i>

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.980
You don't remember anything?

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.770
I found the shining mushrooms in the cave, and then...

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.150
Oh, no!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.400
Did I do something bad?

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.150
It was awful!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.400
Really?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.530
You're lucky you don't remember.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.740
Was it that bad?

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.790
Oh, no, poor Nadia! You don't remember a thing?

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.750
I feel so good!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.460
I never expected I could take a shower here.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.300
It was my invention.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.430
I want to take one too.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.390
It's amazing, Jean. You certainly are a genius.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.270
Genius is one percent inspiration, ninety-nine percent perspiration.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.230
Who said that?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.440
The great inventor, Jean Rocque Raltique.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.230
Jean... Roc...

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:56.940
Your relative?

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.320
It's me!

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.950
Geez...

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.910
I wanted to say it before someone else does.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.830
Here, Nadia, wash your hair with this.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.870
You have shampoo too?

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.540
Not ordinary shampoo.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.130
This is made of seaweed, so you don't need to rinse.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.130
Oh, no! Jean, you naughty boy!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.430
Naughty? Nadia's acting funny again.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.100
What's going on now?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.780
Jean, the shower has stopped.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.950
I'm sorry. It's broken.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.040
It will take time to repair it.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.050
Oh, well, it can't be helped.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.100
But it was very good. Thank you!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.680
I'll try the shampoo when you repair it, Jean.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.440
She usually gets angry.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.770
She must have eaten something strange again.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.110
Say, Jean, how do I look?

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.450
I made this myself. Do you think it's nice?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.910
Made it yourself?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.620
What happened to the curtain?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.580
Say I look nice!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.050
Yes, very nice!

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.880
Thank you, Jean!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:50.010
Wait! Don't you run away from me!

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.230
He's so fast!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:57.900
All right then! Here's the last try! Go!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.910
How was that?

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.490
You're too young to get away.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.210
Evil never wins.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.880
You just keep quiet, and do what I say!

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.900
King! King!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.780
Let's play Gratan now!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.330
Marie will be the Gratan and King will be the human tank!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:55.370
It's fun! It's fun!

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.390
It's become so peaceful.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.520
Marie and King are still good friends.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.520
Nadia has finally become sociable.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:25.610
It seems our days on the Nautilus are far behind us.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.910
Are we going to stay on this island long?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.160
Are we going to live on this island forever?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.170
Okay! I'll talk to her tonight!

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.130
Jean!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.920
No, it's now! Now is the time!

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.140
If you put this to your ear...

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.640
Nadia, I want to...

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.720
I can't hear.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.930
I can hear the sound of ocean.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.360
Will you try?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.160
See? Can you hear it? The sound of the waves?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.220
All right! It's fixed now! Ready, Nadia?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.220
Wait a second!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.220
I'm ready now.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.470
Here I go!

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.060
Won't it stop again?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.360
It's all right this time.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.610
Why?

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.570
Because I'm moving it.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:55.070
Well? Can you see?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:58.330
I can see, but not very well.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:00.200
That's funny.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.420
Yeah, it's not clear at all!

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.000
What? No lens!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.840
That happened because there's nothing to secure the lens.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.510
Now you can see it.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.470
I can't see it.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.730
Move it to the right.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.520
How is it?

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.520
I can see it! It moved?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.690
The Earth did.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.190
Not the moon?

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:32.530
The Earth rotates on its axis once a day,

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.910
so it looks like the moon is moving.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.370
Rotates?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:40.490
The scientist Copernicus figured it out,

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.620
and then Galileo proved it. It is called the heliocentric theory.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.500
Everybody believed that the sun,

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:51.800
the moon and the stars were moving before the theory was formed.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.720
Galileo proved the theory using the telescope.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.550
He was persecuted by the people.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.560
Am I boring you?

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.770
No! You know everything, Jean.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.730
Oh, not at all.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.480
I still have so much to learn.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:16.450
But we depend upon you for our very survival.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:21.870
Without you, I...

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.330
Nadia...

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.630
I promise I'll take you to where you were born someday.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.170
Jean...

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.800
Nadia...

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.930
Actually, that was my first time.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.640
My first time to kiss a girl.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.140
How about you, Nadia?

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.520
Why?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.610
I was just curious.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.650
My second time!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.070
Who was the first one?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.320
The one who was beside me.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.620
Beside you? Was it Sanson?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.290
No, it wasn't!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.660
It couldn't have been Hanson?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.000
You've got to be joking!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.870
The chief navigator?

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.210
What are you talking about?

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.840
Yeah! The helmsman!

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:53.460
Stop it!

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.210
The engineer!

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:54.800
No!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.750
The targeting crewman?

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:56.300
No!

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.510
The leveling crewman?

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:57.920
No!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.590
I got it! The chief of the science department!

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.390
Cut it out!

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.930
You're rude to ask a girl such a question!

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.390
I'm sorry.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:11.600
I regret I kissed such a rotten boy in the first place!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:17.030
You don't remember a thing!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.490
Jean, you jerk!

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:29.370
Oh, no! Poor Nadia! You don't remember it!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.040
The mushrooms...

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:38.840
Oh my god, I'm such an idiot!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.150
Good morning, King.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.990
What is it? Are you sick?

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.200
Jean, wake up!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.040
Has King turned into a log?

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.080
What are these?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.580
A message?

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.250
He left it?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.460
Can you read it, Nadia?

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.760
Let me see...

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.920
What did he say?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.720
As I'm an animal, I'm going back to the world of animals

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.180
to think about myself for a while.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.220
He's left us!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:11.140
Hey!

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.310
King!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.650
Where did he go?

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.070
I didn't expect this island to be so large.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.610
Yes, it has caves too.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.650
Caves?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.320
There are lots of mushrooms.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.950
Mushrooms?

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.490
It's nothing!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:34.960
I tried to forget about that! Darn you, Jean!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:41.840
I'm sorry, Nadia! Please forgive me! Okay?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.510
You're so pathetic. Don't follow me!

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:45.470
But...

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:51.390
Let's search separately. Marie and I will search in these woods.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.770
You look for him on that mountain, Jean!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:59.560
What? You're a male! It must be easy for you!

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.190
Let's go, Marie!

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.280
Wait up!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.530
Easy for me?

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.790
Where did King go?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.330
I'll try my super powers.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.750
Super powers?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.880
I have the power to communicate with animals.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.210
Really?

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.340
Here goes.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.470
Find him?

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.220
No, no answer.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.220
Can you really do that?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.430
I was cold to King.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.190
Marie was mean to King too.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.530
I wish I had greater power.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:54.660
I could search for him easily if I had an airplane.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.500
If I was smarter, I could invent various things.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:01.380
Maybe I can make an airplane to get us off the island.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:04.920
With that, I could take Nadia to Africa.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.590
Maybe then she'd go back to being happy.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.590
I'll have to build it to carry Marie and King too.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.350
But there's no runway on this island.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.520
There'd be no place to take off from.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.440
I have to make a water plane.

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.610
Right! I'll hurry and make one so we can all leave!

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.580
That was close. I was almost killed!

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:48.800
What was I doing?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.930
My gosh, it's a mineral vein!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:03.020
It's...

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.940
Oil!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.930
Thank you for waiting! I'll explain it to you now!

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:47.310
This is a super long wave TV using diodes and a permanent magnet.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.910
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.410
A super-cooled excavator that uses a centrifugal heavy oil engine

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.540
and a hydraulic cylinder.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.460
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.720
This is a high-speed rotary recorder that records sounds

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.930
by changing them into electric signals using a magnet.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:29.230
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:37.530
An electronic brain that calculates with electric signals.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.790
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.250
This is a compression propeller

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:56.630
that gets its propellant force by burning jet fuel.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.850
Here is a laminated integrated circuit

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.850
made with silicon resins found in common dirt.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:10.440
This a construction robot employing a pocket motor

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.110
and magnetic recording repetition system.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.280
This is an electromagnetic telephoto antenna

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.200
that receives radio waves from space.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.040
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.880
This is a graphite channel hearth that works

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.460
by reacting with an isotope.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:39.130
This is an artificial sun that turns night into day.

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.440
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:19:00.700
I certainly am a real genius!

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.790
Please come this way, Princess.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.920
Where are we going?

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.880
To her highness' homeland.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.920
Etoile de la Seine X, launch!

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.980
Incredible, Jean! You certainly are a genius!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.190
Setting auto-pilot. Destination, the African continent.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.740
My dream has come true at last!

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.280
Thank you, Jean!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.280
You're wrong, Nadia. This is my dream!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.490
Where is King?

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.210
He is in the circus in Paris.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:35.960
No! We left him on that island!

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:40.130
Jean, go back to the island! We must take King with us!

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:45.180
It's too late. I've set the automatic control system already.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.430
Please, Jean, go back to the island!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:52.020
I'm sorry, but we can't cancel it once we set it.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.480
Then I'll do it myself!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.320
No, don't touch that! That's...

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.030
A self-destruct device!

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.660
That uses gunpowder!

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.340
Where am I?

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.380
My airplane...

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.960
Nadia? Marie?

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.720
My airplane failed after all.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.850
Why did it fail?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:34.480
I always fail. I'm just...

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.850
Don't give up!

00:21:37.350 --> 00:21:38.860
Captain Nemo!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:42.730
Today's mistake is tomorrow's success.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:47.990
You must develop your capacities with a strong will and belief.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.830
Captain Nemo...

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:57.790
Genius is one percent inspiration, ninety-nine percent perspiration.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:04.050
That was said by the great American inventor, Thomas Edison.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:09.760
Remember those words and make Nadia's dream come true.

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:13.970
Commander Nemo!

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.980
Don't call me commander!

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:20.400
Captain Nemo!

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:25.400
Captain Nemo... Captain Nemo...

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.150
What?

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:35.540
It was just a dream?

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:44.750
King!

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:47.340
King must have been jealous.

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:48.260
Jealous?

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:51.510
Because Jean and you became intimate.

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:53.180
Me?

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:55.430
He knows everything.

00:22:57.430 --> 00:22:59.900
Do you love Jean, Nadia?

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.400
I don't know.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:04.230
You're cute, Nadia!

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:05.030
Why is that?

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:08.950
You don't even know what your own feelings are.

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:10.240
Marie!

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:12.160
Your face turned red!

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.750
Because of the sunset! Where did you learn that kind of thing?

00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:25.670
King!

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:33.090
I'm sorry! I'm sorry, King!

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:39.680
What's the matter, Jean?

00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:43.190
My glasses fall down when I'm happy.

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:45.820
That's strange!

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.740
When I'm happy, my glasses fall down.
